X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Livewhale": "https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/18069-best-practices-for-working-with-lgbtqia2s-patients"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:Best Practices for Working with LGBTQIA2S+ Patients Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T170000
DTSTAMP:20260417T121016Z
UID:20260428T220000Z-18069@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T150000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,500,500/607_cs_-_best_practices_distr._cal._img..rev
 .1776802625.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events,Student Government,Student Services
DESCRIPTION:This training helps future health providers deliver LGBTQIA+ i
 nclusive care by teaching affirming language\, respectful communication\, 
 and key clinical considerations such as working with patients who use bind
 ers or hormone therapy.  It also covers how to create stigma-free environm
 ents\, address microaggressions\, and practice real-world scenarios\, equi
 pping students with skills to provide safe\, affirming patient experiences
 .  Tuesday\, April 28  3:30–5 PM  Lindley Center\, Room 396  Food provid
 ed  All SRJC community members are welcome\, come learn\, reflect\, and gr
 ow together.RSVP here! (https://santarosajuniorcollege.formstack.com/forms
 /bestpracticesforlgbtqia2s)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260421T202314Z
LOCATION:Lindley STEM Center\, room 396 - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/18069-best-practices-for-working-
 with-lgbtqia2s-patients
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This training helps future health provid
 ers deliver LGBTQIA+ inclusive care by teaching affirming language\, respe
 ctful communication\, and key clinical considerations such as working with
  patients who use binders or hormone therapy.</p><p>  It also covers how t
 o create stigma-free environments\, address microaggressions\, and practic
 e real-world scenarios\, equipping students with skills to provide safe\, 
 affirming patient experiences.</p><p>  Tuesday\, April 28<br />  3:30–5 
 PM<br />  Lindley Center\, Room 396<br />  Food provided</p><p>  All SRJC 
 community members are welcome\, come learn\, reflect\, and grow together.<
 /p><p><a href="https://santarosajuniorcollege.formstack.com/forms/bestprac
 ticesforlgbtqia2s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RSVP here!</a></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:18069
