BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Livewhale": "https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/18349-totally-a-one-woman-show-of-healing-humor-and"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:TOTALLY: A One-Woman Show of Healing\, Humor\, and Transformation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T200000
DTSTAMP:20260423T155606Z
UID:20260429T010000Z-18349@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260428T180000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,710,710/609_cs_-_totally_SHS_show.rev.1776984962.png
CATEGORIES:Student Services
DESCRIPTION:Kimleigh Smith\, an actress and survivor\, created her one-wom
 an show TOTALLY based on her journey of healing after sexual assault. Thro
 ugh storytelling\, humor\, and performance\, she explores trauma\, recover
 y\, and empowerment while challenging stigma and encouraging open conversa
 tions. Her work inspires others to reclaim their voice\, embrace their pow
 er\, and transform pain into growth—what she calls "embracing your cape.
 "&#160\;  Free admission and parking!  For more information\, visit the St
 udent Health Services Events website here! (https://shs.santarosa.edu/tota
 lly)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260423T225606Z
LOCATION:Newman Auditorium - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/18349-totally-a-one-woman-show-of
 -healing-humor-and
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Kimleigh Smith\, an actress and survivor
 \, created her one-woman show TOTALLY based on her journey of healing afte
 r sexual assault. Through storytelling\, humor\, and performance\, she exp
 lores trauma\, recovery\, and empowerment while challenging stigma and enc
 ouraging open conversations. Her work inspires others to reclaim their voi
 ce\, embrace their power\, and transform pain into growth—what she calls
  "embracing your cape."&#160\;</p><p>  Free admission and parking!</p><p> 
  For more information\, <a href="https://shs.santarosa.edu/totally" target
 ="_blank" rel="noopener">visit the Student Health Services Events website 
 here!</a></p>
