DESCRIPTION:Join the SRJC Disability Cultural Center (DCC) and Queer Resou
 rce Center (QRC) for an afternoon of connection\, creativity\, and communi
 ty! Disabled &amp\; Queer Joy Night is a low-pressure mixer designed for d
 isabled and queer folks (and those who live at the intersection of both) t
 o come together\, relax\, and celebrate joy in all its forms.  Come hang o
 ut\, meet new people\, and enjoy:Snacks and refreshments  Chill crafts and
  creative activities  Games and casual fun  A welcoming\, affirming space 
 to just be    Whether you're looking to make new friends\, connect with co
 mmunity\, or simply unwind in a space that celebrates you—you belong her
 e.  April 29th  3:00–5:00 PM  SRJC Intercultural Center\, Pioneer Hall\,
  Room 380  This event is open to students\, staff\, community members\, an
 d anyone in between. Bring yourself\, bring a friend\, or come solo—ther
 e's space for you here.  For more information\, visit the DCC website here
 ! (https://drd.santarosa.edu/dcc)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260324T213139Z
LOCATION:Intercultural Center\, Pioneer Hall\, Room 380 - Santa Rosa Campu
 s
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/17032-disabled-queer-joy-night
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the SRJC Disability Cultural Center
  (DCC) and Queer Resource Center (QRC) for an afternoon of connection\, cr
 eativity\, and community! Disabled &amp\; Queer Joy Night is a low-pressur
 e mixer designed for disabled and queer folks (and those who live at the i
 ntersection of both) to come together\, relax\, and celebrate joy in all i
 ts forms.</p><p>  Come hang out\, meet new people\, and enjoy:</p><ul><li>
 Snacks and refreshments  </li><li>Chill crafts and creative activities  </
 li><li>Games and casual fun  </li><li>A welcoming\, affirming space to jus
 t be  </li></ul><p>  Whether you're looking to make new friends\, connect 
 with community\, or simply unwind in a space that celebrates you—you bel
 ong here.</p><p>  April 29th<br />  3:00–5:00 PM<br />  SRJC Intercultur
 al Center\, Pioneer Hall\, Room 380</p><p>  This event is open to students
 \, staff\, community members\, and anyone in between. Bring yourself\, bri
 ng a friend\, or come solo—there's space for you here.</p><p>  For more 
 information\, <a href="https://drd.santarosa.edu/dcc" target="_blank" rel=
 "noopener">visit the DCC website here!</a></p>
