ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,720,720/408_Library_workshop_Calendar_image.rev.1756
 417994.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an informative\, non-partisan session designed to 
 help new and old voters feel comfortable and prepared for the voting proce
 ss.  Hear from The Sonoma County Registrar of Voters\, representatives fro
 m The League of Women Voters\, and the Office of Assemblymen Chris Rogers.
  This session will walk through how voting works\, what to expect\, and ho
 w to participate with confidence.  Some instructors are offering extra cre
 dit for attendance.  Open to the public.  No pre-registration required.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260423T202210Z
LOCATION:Doyle Library\, Room 146 - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/18342-your-vote-matters
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join us for an informative\, non-partisa
 n session designed to help new and old voters feel comfortable and prepare
 d for the voting process.</p><p>  Hear from The Sonoma County Registrar of
  Voters\, representatives from The League of Women Voters\, and the Office
  of Assemblymen Chris Rogers. This session will walk through how voting wo
 rks\, what to expect\, and how to participate with confidence.<br />  Some
  instructors are offering extra credit for attendance.</p><p>  Open to the
  public.<br />  No pre-registration required.</p>
