BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Petaluma Chamber of Commerce": "https://business.petalumachamber.us/events/details/free-estate-planning-webinar-05-07-2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:petaluma_chamber
SUMMARY:Free Estate Planning Webinar
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T183000
UID:d0d4984efef5750d842cf0798189b023@growthzone.com
DESCRIPTION:Details Strategies to Manage Incapacity\, Family Dynamics\, an
 d Financial Risks creating your estate plan\, whether it’s a living trus
 t or a will\, can be a daunting task. Estate planning addresses issues tha
 t are difficult to think about\, such as death\, incapacity\, finances\, a
 nd family dynamics. It can be easy to procrastinate\, even though these is
 sues may weigh heavily on your mind. We invite you to attend one of our up
 coming free webinars so you can take the first step toward having peace of
  mind by creating (or updating) your estate plan. This is an educational w
 ebinar\, where we highlight some of the concerns that many families face a
 nd how an estate plan can help. The attorneys also break down how wills an
 d trusts differ\, and some of the common estate planning pitfalls and how 
 to avoid them. Our goal is to provide you with the education you need to p
 rotect yourself and your family\, and leave a legacy of peace. If you woul
 d like to set up a meeting to discuss your estate planning needs
LOCATION:Petaluma\, CA
URL:https://business.petalumachamber.us/events/details/free-estate-plannin
 g-webinar-05-07-2026
X-SOURCE:Petaluma Chamber of Commerce
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Petaluma Arts Center": "https://petalumaartscenter.org/events-exhibitions/origins-story"}
X-SOURCE-ID:petaluma_arts_center
SUMMARY:The Threads That Connect Us
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260507T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T160000
UID:ebd76bdfb70deb09e1f9484e6bcbe433@petalumaartscenter.org
DESCRIPTION:“Gaining From My Parents’ Loss” by Jorge de la Cal The T
 hreads That Connect Us Exhibition Dates: May 7 - June 6\, 2026 Opening Rec
 eption: Thursday\, May 7\, 5:30-7:30pm The Threads That Connect Us\, an ex
 hibition from the Origin Stories Project that weaves together storytelling
  and visual art to explore identity\, connection\, and the shared human ex
 perience. Each of the 70 works begins with a personal story—an identity-
 shaping moment of legacy\, arrival\, adversity\, or revelation. These narr
 atives are then transformed into Stories + Art Boxes using plexiglass encl
 osures where voice and visual expression are experienced together. At its 
 core\, the project is grounded in a simple belief: when people share their
  stories and truly listen to one another\, connection grows. This exhibiti
 on brings together works from the permanent collection alongside a Gen Z s
 howcase featuring Northern California students. The Gen Z component offers
  an intergenerational perspective on resilience\, self-discovery\, and bel
 onging. #block-635d83d9438605f6fa53 { --tweak-text-block-radius: 0px 0px 0
 px 0px\; --tweak-text-block-radius: unset\; --stroke-style: none\;--stroke
 -thickness: 6px\; --tweak-text-block-background-color: initial\; } #block-
 635d83d9438605f6fa53 .sqs-html-content { --tweak-text-block-padding: 6% 6%
