X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_sonoma_county_go_wild_hikers
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Go Wild Hikers
UID:event_314407679@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260426T035102Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260509T113000
SUMMARY:Vista Trail at Sugarloaf
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers\nWe never get tired of hiking Sugarloaf. This i
 s a very popular park with rolling hills\, dense forests\, creeks\, wildfl
 owers & waterfalls (in season). We'll hike up to Vista Trail while taking 
 in the beauty. Then hike back down past Sonoma Creek. Appropriate for indi
 viduals with at least a moderate level of fitness.\n\n**\\*Important Notic
 e\\***\nIf you've enjoyed hiking with this group follow me as I move Go Wi
 ld Hikers to a new platform called Heylo at - [https://www.heylo.com/](htt
 ps://www.heylo.com/)\n\n**Where We Meet/Important Directions**\nSugarloaf 
 Ridge State Park\n2605 Adobe Canyon Road\, Kenwood\, 95452\n**Get there Ea
 rly! Carpool if you can - This is a very Popular Park!**\nGive yourself en
 ough time to arrive\, use the restroom & pay park fee. It often takes long
 er than you think.\n**Meet in large parking lot on the left after passing 
 entrance/Pay Kiosk!**\n\n**The Hike (Group Hike #342)**\nLower Bald Mtn\, 
 Bald Mountain\, Vista\, Meadow and Creekside Nature Trails - a loop hike\n
 Distance - +/-4.75 miles/+/-7.6 kilometers\nElevation change - +/-800 feet
 /+/-244 meters\nDifficulty - 7/10 moderate with some steep sections\nExpos
 ures - 40% shade/60 % sun - rocky\, poison oak\, ticks and insects\nBring 
 plenty of water - at least 34 oz./ 1 liter\nDogs - Not permitted\nFaciliti
 es at trail head - shade\, picnic tables and toilets\nCost - $5 cash\nPark
 ing - $10 State Park fee or free with your State Park Pass.\nRemember to w
 ear appropriate hiking shoes\, bring plenty of water\, a hat\, a snack and
  layered clothing.\nPlease Do Not Use Any scented products the day of a gr
 oup hike!\nOf course we will all look out for each other but ultimately\, 
 hikers are responsible for their own safety and well-being during hikes.\n
 \nSarmentine French Bakery/Cafe\n(Near McDonald's)\n52 Mission Circle\, Su
 ite # 112\nSanta Rosa\, CA 95409\n[(707) 623-9595](https://www.google.com/
 search?q=sarmentine+alexandra&source=lmns&bih=768&biw=1342&client=safari&h
 l=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwizy6KH0v6AAxWsIkQIHb4UA3cQ0pQJKAB6BAgBEAI#)\n[https:/
 /www.sarmentine.com/](https://www.sarmentine.com/)\n\n**When We Meet**\nSa
 turday May 9\, 2026\n8:30 am - 11:30 am\n**Get there Early! Carpool if you
  can - This is a very Popular Park!**\nIf your plans change after you sign
  up even if you're on the waitlist\, please update your RSVP.\nDo Not Atte
 nd if you are sick\, running a fever\, were exposed to or have tested posi
 tive for Covid-19 or any other contagion!\nHike may be changed\, reschedul
 ed or cancelled in case of excessive heat\, rain\, smoke/AQI\, illness\, z
 ombie apocalypse etc... Check your email the night before for any possible
  changes.\n\n**Notice to New Hikers Only**\n**"When a New Hiker (never hik
 ed with me before) doesn't show up (No Show) to their first hike with the 
 group\, they will be removed (not banned) from the group immediately."**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/sonoma-county-go-wild-hikers/events/3
 14407679/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260421T232036Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260421T232036Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
